! The index flag and index RESULT indicators, for the immediate index
! operations that were not setting them.
!
! Ref. Manual p.25, directly under SUBTRACT IMMEDIATE FROM COUNT: "The
! index flag and index result indicators are set in all of the
! preceding immediate index arithmetic operations. The index comparison
! indicators are not changed."  "All of the preceding" covers LVI,
! LVNI, LCI, LRI, V+I.., V-I.., C+I and C-I.  Six of those set nothing
! in this model until pp.24-25 were read: LVI, LVNI, LCI, LRI, C+I and
! C-I.
!
! WHY THIS IS HAND-WRITTEN rather than transcribed, which is the
! exception here and wants justifying.  C-I got its witness from the
! deck -- jb_ax4b routine 1238 test 3 does C-I then BXCZ back to back,
! and without the fix that loop never ends.  LVI got one by accident,
! from the I/O test's whole-indicator-word check.  For the other four
! there is no deck witness to find: the diagnostics verify a count or
! value by COMPARING it (KC/KV, which set the COMPARISON indicators)
! and branching on that, not by branching on the operation's own result
! indicators.  jb_ax4b routine 1236, a whole routine "Checks C+I and
! C-I", is built that way throughout -- C+I, then KC, then BXE.  So
! these four are fixed on the manual's authority, and this program is
! what keeps that honest.  It is manual-derived, NOT deck-derived, and
! that is the weaker of the two standards used in this suite.
!
! Each test clears the indicator register first, so the indicator it
! then branches on must have been turned on by the operation under
! test.  Without the fix the branch is not taken and the program halts
! on the FAIL line naming the operation.
!
! MEASURED, one injection per operation, each removing only that arm's
! setIndexResultIndicatorsF call.  Every one halts on ITS OWN failure
! line, so the four tests are independent rather than one firing four
! times:
!
!   LVNI  halts 002101.40      LRI  halts 002105.40
!   LCI   halts 002103.40      C+I  halts 002107.40
!   (PASS is 002110.00)
!
! AND THE FIRST RUN OF THOSE INJECTIONS WAS INERT, which is worth more
! than the result.  All four reported "injected" and all four PASSED.
! The harness sliced each arm up to the following "end", so the arm's
! last line carried NO trailing newline, while the removal pattern
! included one -- the replace matched nothing and the script still said
! it had worked.  The assert checked only that the call was PRESENT
! beforehand, never that it was GONE after.  Four silent no-ops
! reported as four successful injections, and a green result meaning
! nothing.  The fixed harness asserts the call is absent afterwards.
! Same failure as the refill-gate control that passed because the entry
! point skipped half the block: when a control comes back green,
! suspect the control.
!
! NOT COVERED: XF.  Every index word here has flag 0, so the tests pin
! the result indicators only.  A word with the flag set, loaded and
! then branched on with BXF, would add it.

        SLC, (8)2100.0
START   Z, $IND
        LVNI, $X1, 1                 ! value := -(1 << 5), negative
        BXVLZ, T2                    ! LVNI must turn on XVLZ
        BEW, $                       ! FAIL: LVNI set no result indicators

T2      Z, $IND
        LCI, $X1, 0                  ! count := 0
        BXCZ, T3                     ! LCI must turn on XCZ
        BEW, $                       ! FAIL: LCI set no result indicators

T3      Z, $IND
        LRI, $X1, 4                  ! refill := 4; value still negative
        BXVLZ, T4                    ! LRI must turn on XVLZ
        BEW, $                       ! FAIL: LRI set no result indicators

T4      Z, $IND
        C+I, $X1, 0                  ! count := 0 + 0, still zero
        BXCZ, PASS                   ! C+I must turn on XCZ
        BEW, $                       ! FAIL: C+I set no result indicators

PASS    BEW, $
        END, START
